{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-ea2f7f347da83804c0db","statement":"\\Delta\nB_{11}=XJ_m(0)-(J_n(\\mu)^{-T}-\\lambda\nI_n)X\n\n=\n\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n0&x_{11}&\\dots&x_{1,m-1} \\\\\n0&x_{21}&\\dots&x_{2,m-1} \\\\\n0&x_{31}&\\dots&x_{3,m-1} \\\\\n\\hdotsfor{4}\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\n+\\lambda^2\n\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n0&\\dots&0 \\\\\nx_{11}&\\dots&x_{1m} \\\\\nx_{21}&\\dots&x_{2m} \\\\\n\\hdotsfor{3}\\\\\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\n-\\lambda^3\n\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n0&\\dots&0 \\\\\n0&\\dots&0 \\\\\nx_{11}&\\dots&x_{1m} \\\\\n\\hdotsfor{3}\\\\\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\n+\\cdots,","source_id":"arXiv:1004.3584","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"9c206059c193269748eecfd8b25bebca789c28718c09f7358d90d3940b37545a","kind":"equation","label":"Equation kif","ref_key":"kif","name":"","order":56,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.3584","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"da7694bd01118586f2d942a776eec1e2d33ddd2c07a7a628e5c9e0454c9479b3","line":2673,"origin":"latex_env:equation","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:49+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":415,"math_hints":42}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1004.3584","title":"Miniversal deformations of matrices of bilinear forms","abstract":"V.I. Arnold [Russian Math. Surveys 26 (2) (1971) 29-43] constructed a miniversal deformation of matrices under similarity; that is, a simple normal form to which not only a given square matrix A but all matrices B close to it can be reduced by similarity transformations that smoothly depend on the entries of B. We construct a miniversal deformation of matrices under congruence.","authors":["Andrii R. Dmytryshyn","Vyacheslav Futorny","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2010","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.3584","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"le":"\\leqslant","ge":"\\geqslant"},"macros_override